comments.text:
Description:
Run these queries:

PREPARE p0 FROM 'CREATE TABLE t1 (c0 INT) PARTITION BY HASH(-NULL)';
EXECUTE p0;
-- ERROR 1486 (HY000): Constant, random or timezone-dependent expressions in (sub)partitioning function are not allowed (expected error)
EXECUTE p0;
-- Assertion error at sql/item_func.cc:403
-- assert(fixed == 0 || basic_const_item());

However if `-` is removed from the CREATE statement:

PREPARE p0 FROM 'CREATE TABLE t1 (c0 INT) PARTITION BY HASH(NULL)';
EXECUTE p0;
-- ERROR 1486 (HY000): Constant, random or timezone-dependent expressions in (sub)partitioning function are not allowed (expected error)
EXECUTE p0;
-- No error

The second EXECUTE is successful when it shouldn't.

The compilation parameters are the same as issue 108148:

-DWITH_DEBUG=1 -DWITH_ASAN=ON -DWITH_UBSAN=ON and boost library version 1.77

How to repeat:
Run the statements above.
